 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 531804,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/712256fe40261b0a.jpg\" alt=\"\">\n(credit: modification of work by Ren, Liyan et al./PloS one)\n</figure>",
   "stem_html": "<p>The graph shows serotonin levels on two groups of mice. The \"KO\" group mice have depression (artificially induced for the study) and the \"Con\" group is the control group.</p>\n<p>What is a conclusion that can be drawn from this graph?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1040132,
     "content_html": "Mice with depression do not produce any serotonin."
    },
    {
     "id": 1040133,
     "content_html": "Mice with depression produce the same amounts of serotonin as other mice."
    },
    {
     "id": 1040134,
     "content_html": "Mice with depression produce more serotonin than other mice."
    },
    {
     "id": 1040135,
     "content_html": "Mice with depression produce less serotonin than other mice."
    }
   ],
